<title>CANADA: Bombardier in $176 million Mexico subway deal.</title>
<headline>Bombardier in $176 million Mexico subway deal.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc. said Tuesday its Mexican unit signed a contract valued at C$176 million ($129.4 million) to refurbish 256 subway cars for Mexico City's transit authority.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Bombardier-Concarril SA de CV will refurbish 28 subway train sets of nine cars each, plus four spare cars, at its Sahagun plant, located near Mexico City.</p>
<p>Deliveries should begin in the fall of 1997 and will be spread over 25 months, Bombardier said.</p>
</text>
